ngly","affectless","affector","disaffect","interaffect","misaffect","overaffect","reaffect","unaffect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f6a07b86153c63b45c","definition":"To feign or pretend.","example":"The light above the door made it unconvincing to affect that no one was at home.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["affectability","affectable","affectee","affectingly","affectless","affector","disaffect","interaffect","misaffect","overaffect","reaffect","unaffect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:06e74bba70ca1240a6","definition":"To make a show of; to put on a pretense of; to feign; to assume. To make a false display of.","example":"to affect ignorance","pos":"verb","synonyms":["fake","simulate","feign"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["affectability","affectable","affectee","affectingly","affectless","affector","disaffect","interaffect","misaffect","overaffect","reaffect","unaffect","affected","affectedly","affectedness","affectation","affecter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bc6f58a77a50e38c47","definition":"To aim for, to try to obtain.","example":"Duke.[...] I loue the people,\nBut doe not like to stage me to their eyes:\nThough it doe well, I doe not rellish well\nTheir lowd applause, and Aues vehement:\nNor doe I thinke the man of safe discretion\nThat do's affect it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["affectability","affectable","affectee","affectingly","affectless","affector","disaffect","interaffect","misaffect","overaffect","reaffect","unaffect","affected","affectedly","affectedness","affectation","affecter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea49207da0f08af0df","definition":"To feel affection for (someone); to like, be fond of.","example":"There is a Lady in Verona heere\nWhom I affect: but she is nice, and coy,\nAnd naught esteemes my aged eloquence.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare","register":"rare, transitive","wordFamily":["affectability","affectable","affectee","affectingly","affectless","affector","disaffect","interaffect","misaffect","overaffect","reaffect","unaffect","affected","affectedly","affectedness","affectation","affecter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d7a0154a4e94e21add","definition":"To show a fondness for (something); to choose.","example":"Amongst humane conditions this one is very common, that we are rather pleased with strange things then with our owne; we love changes, affect alterations, and like innovations.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["affectability","affectable","affectee","affectingly","affectless","affector","disaffect","interaffect","misaffect","overaffect","reaffect","unaffect","affected","affectedly","affectedness","affectation","affecter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kai